import BlogArticle from "../../components/BlogArticle.astro";
---

<BlogArticle
	title="PAN Card Reprint Steps: How to Request a Replacement Card"
	description="Learn when to request a PAN card reprint, how Protean’s current reprint service works, and when to choose a correction request instead."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/blogs/pan-card-reprint/"
	heading="PAN card reprint steps"
	intro="If your PAN card is lost, damaged, or you need another physical copy, a reprint may be the right route—as long as the information on your PAN record does not need to change."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">When to request a reprint</h2>
		<p>
			A reprint issues a replacement PAN card with the existing PAN
			details. It is not a new PAN application and does not correct a
			name, address, date of birth, photo, or signature in the record.
			If any details must be updated, start with the provider’s
			change/correction service instead.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Protean’s separate online reprint route</h2>
		<p>
			Protean states that its separate online reprint facility is for
			PAN holders whose latest PAN application was processed through
			Protean or the Income Tax Department e-Filing portal, and only
			when no data change is required. Its published guidance says this
			request does not require an application form or supporting
			documents; the service may ask for verification and payment
			details during the live process.
		</p>
		<ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li>Open the official <a class="text-link" href="https://onlineservices.proteantech.in/paam/ReprintEPan.html">Protean e-PAN/PAN reprint service</a> and read its eligibility conditions.</li>
			<li>Enter the requested PAN and contact details, then complete the displayed verification step.</li>
			<li>Confirm the address and delivery option presented by the portal. Check any current fee before paying.</li>
			<li>Submit the request and save the acknowledgement or reference number for tracking.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>
			Eligibility, address rules, charges, and delivery options may
			change. If the separate reprint service says the PAN is not
			eligible, use the provider’s official instructions for an
			alternative; do not create a second PAN application.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Use the correct provider’s route</h2>
		<p>
			UTIITSL provides its own reprint facility. Start at its official
			PAN services site and follow the current “Reprint PAN Card”
			option; do not assume Protean’s eligibility rules or steps apply
			to a UTIITSL-processed record. If you are unsure which provider
			processed the original request, check the PAN application
			acknowledgement or use the official provider guidance.
		</p>
	</section>

	<p>
		For Protean’s current service description, see
		<a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/pan-index.html">PAN application and reprint options</a>.
		For UTIITSL, start at the <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pan.utiitsl.com/">official UTIITSL PAN site</a>.
		This website is an independent image-preparation tool, not a PAN
		application or card-issuance service.
	</p>
</BlogArticle>
